.TH LLDPND 8 "October 2026" "lldpnd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lldpnd \- LLDP (IEEE 802.1AB) neighbour discovery daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lldpnd
.B \-i
.IR interface [, interface ...]
.RB [ \-c
.IR interface ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR hold ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR count ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR credit ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR description ]
.RB [ \-P
.IR description ]
.RB [ \-M ]
.RB [ \-S
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-U
.IR user ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lldpnd
implements the Link Layer Discovery Protocol over raw
.B AF_PACKET
sockets.
On each interface it periodically transmits an LLDPDU describing this
system to the nearest-bridge group address 01:80:C2:00:00:0E, and keeps a
table of the neighbours it hears, removing each one when its advertised
time-to-live expires or when it sends a shutdown LLDPDU.
.PP
Advertised TLVs: Chassis ID (MAC address of the chassis interface, the
same on every port), Port ID (interface name), TTL, Port Description,
System Name, System Description, System Capabilities, Management Address
(the interface's first IPv4 and IPv6 address, else its MAC) and End Of
LLDPDU.
.PP
Received LLDPDUs are validated strictly and discarded if malformed:
TLV lengths that run past the frame, missing or misordered mandatory
TLVs, reserved Chassis/Port ID subtypes, repeated TLVs and illegal
lengths are all rejected.
Unrecognised TLV types are counted and skipped.
.PP
Local changes are advertised immediately (rate-limited by the transmit
credit): interface alias, MAC, IP addresses, operational state, and the
hostname when
.B \-n
is not given.
When an interface goes down its neighbours are flushed; when it comes
back the daemon re-initialises after a 2-second reinitDelay and starts
with a burst of fast transmissions.
An interface that disappears and reappears with the same name is
re-attached.
.PP
LLDPDUs carrying this system's own chassis ID (another of its ports
bridged to this one) are not recorded; a loop warning is logged once.
.PP
The daemon is single-threaded, event-driven (epoll, timerfd, signalfd,
rtnetlink) and does not wake up unless there is work.
SIGINT or SIGTERM sends a shutdown LLDPDU (TTL 0) on every port, prints
the neighbour tables and statistics, and exits with status 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " interface" [, interface ...]
Run LLDP on these interfaces (repeatable, up to 32).
They must exist at start-up.
.TP
.BI \-c " interface"
Use this interface's MAC address as the chassis ID (default: the first
.B \-i
interface).
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
msgTxInterval, the transmit interval (1\-3600, default 30).
.TP
.BI \-H " hold"
msgTxHold (1\-100, default 4).
The advertised TTL is min(65535,
.IR seconds " \(mu " hold
+ 1).
.TP
.BI \-f " count"
txFastInit: number of LLDPDUs sent one second apart at start-up, on link
up, and when a new neighbour is detected (0\-8, default 4; 0 disables
fast transmission).
.TP
.BI \-C " credit"
txCreditMax: maximum number of LLDPDUs sent back-to-back; one more is
allowed per second (1\-10, default 5).
.TP
.BI \-p " seconds"
Print every neighbour table periodically.
By default a port's table is printed whenever it changes.
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
System Name (default: the hostname, followed live).
.TP
.BI \-d " description"
System Description (default: uname output).
.TP
.BI \-P " description"
Port Description for every port (default: the interface alias, else
the interface name).
.TP
.B \-M
Do not send Management Address TLVs.
.TP
.BI \-S " path"
Control socket for
.BR lldpnd\-ctl (8)
(default
.IR /run/lldpnd.sock ;
.B none
disables it).
If the default path cannot be used the daemon continues without it.
.TP
.BI \-U " user"
After opening its sockets, switch to
.IR user ,
drop all supplementary groups and every capability except
.BR CAP_NET_RAW ,
and set no_new_privs.
.SH OUTPUT
Events are logged to standard output, one per line, with a millisecond
timestamp and the port:
.PP
.nf
.RS
12:00:01.250 [eth0] NEIGHBOUR ADD chassis=02:00:00:00:00:02 port=eth0(st5) name=sw1 ttl=121
12:02:03.001 [eth0] NEIGHBOUR AGEOUT chassis=... (TTL expired, last rx 121000 ms ago)
12:03:00.010 [eth0] rx: discard from 02:00:00:00:00:99: third TLV is not TTL
.RE
.fi
.PP
Every string received from the network is escaped before it is printed.
.SH STANDARDS
IEEE Std 802.1AB-2016, Station and Media Access Control Connectivity
Discovery.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lldpnd\-ctl (8),
.BR packet (7),
.BR rtnetlink (7)
